---
description: WebAPI controller conventions (thin controllers over BusinessLogic services)
globs: SET.WebAPI/Controllers/**/*.cs,SET.WebAPI/Helpers/**/*.cs,SET.BusinessLogic/Models/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

# API controllers

- Inherit `BaseController`; inject via `IServiceProvider` and resolve feature services (`I…Service`) in the ctor
- Controllers stay thin: no `AppDbContext`/`IMapper`; call a `SET.BusinessLogic` service and map its `ServiceResult` with `ToActionResult(...)` (pass `onSuccess` for `Created`/`NoContent`)
- Wrap actions in `TryCatchAsync` (user-scoped overload for authenticated work); pass `RequestDeviceId` as `originDeviceId` for writes
- Prefer `[Authorize(AuthenticationSchemes = JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)]` on controllers that touch user data
- Routes: `[Route("api/…")]` + `[ApiController]`; keep verbs REST-shaped (`HttpGet`/`Post`/`Put`/`Delete`)
- Validation failures return `ServiceError.BadRequest("PascalCaseToken")` from the service, matching existing tokens
- Scope queries with `user.Id`; never trust client-supplied user ids for ownership
- Prefer `DefaultConfigureAwait()` on awaited EF/async calls (project extension)
- DTOs in `SET.BusinessLogic/Models` (`BusinessLogic.Models`); map with helpers or AutoMapper — do not return EF entities
- Request DTO fields clients may omit or send as JSON `null` must be nullable (`string?`, `List<T>?`, …). `SET.BusinessLogic` has `<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`, so non-nullable refs are implicit `[Required]` and `[ApiController]` returns 400 before the action (Flutter chat omits `prompt`, habit save omits `progresses`, title may send null `assistantMessage`)
- AI: keep prompts bounded; never expose `AI_API_KEY` to clients
